\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Find higher-dimensional analogues of the Bonk--Lang theorem on bi-Lipschitz parametrization by Euclidean space, with explicit quantitative control of the bi-Lipschitz constants from the geometric hypotheses. The question asks for a parametrization result, rather than only a continuous or locally topological chart.
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{http://aimpl.org/mappingmetric/3/}{[S2]}.

